\DOC BIGNUM_TERMRANGE_TAC

\TYPE {BIGNUM_TERMRANGE_TAC : term -> term -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Adds a size bound assumption {m < 2 EXP (64 * k)} for a numeric term read as a
{k}-digit bignum in the goal, leaving the conclusion unchanged.

\DESCRIBE
{k} is the digit count used in the bound (a variable or a numeral) and {m} is
the natural-number term to be bounded. The tactic produces one subgoal whose
conclusion and existing assumptions are untouched, with the new assumption
appended at the end of the assumption list; no existing assumption is removed
or modified.
{
           A ?- t
   ======================  BIGNUM_TERMRANGE_TAC k m
   A, m < 2 EXP (64 * k) ?- t
}

\COMMENTS
All observed traces show this single kind of outcome, and in each the
conclusion is an {ensures} specification in which the bounded term appears as
the value of a bignum of {k} digits read from memory.

\ENDDOC
